+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every registered tool declares an `inputSchema` in `src/types/ai.ts` that providers forward to the model, and `ToolRegistry.execute` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` enforces that JSON Schema before any tool executor runs. Validation turns malformed model arguments into a `ToolResponse` the model can read and correct within the existing tool-round budget rather than throwing an unhandled error out of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled when `ToolRegistry.register` runs, and an uncompilable schema throws at registration time with an error message naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static inputSchema at registration, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at registration and reused across `execute` calls rather than recompiled per call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each call and validates against the `inputSchema` current at that call, caching compiled validators by schema object, while valid input carrying unlisted extra properties is passed to the executor unchanged without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults ([validated by: validates dynamic schemas per call and forwards extra keys unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+
+## Execution and error contract
+
+- Before invoking the executor, `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against `required`, declared property types, and `enum`; when validation fails, the executor is never called, a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property paths and failed constraints is returned, and neither the returned `result` nor any log line contains a rejected property value ([validated by: returns a validation result without running the tool or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L29)).
+- Returning a `ToolResponse` on schema failure keeps `ChatOrchestrator` inside its `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` loop so the provider receives the rejection message as a `tool_result` on the next round and can retry with valid arguments ([validated by: feeds a rejected tool call back to the model so a retry can succeed](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name continues to throw `Unknown tool: <name>`, reserving exceptions for lookup failures while input validation failures return a `ToolResponse`.
